<title>SWEDEN: OM, OMLX to cooperate with Norwegian mkts.</title>
<headline>OM, OMLX to cooperate with Norwegian mkts.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish derivatives trader OM, the Oslo Stock Exchange, Norwegian derivatives trader Norsk Opsjonssentral (NOS) and OM's London derivatives trader OMLX will start cooperating on February 14, OM said on Monday.</p>
<p>The cooperation aims to create a common market for Norwegian and Swedish share derivatives that can be reached by more than 120 members in seven countries.</p>
<p>Trading on the three exchanges will be done through a common order book with clearing handled by the single countries' clearing houses through OM, OMLX or NOS.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
